Reading Skill - The concept of reading as a linguistic organization and a vehicle of communication. Reading Problems, Levels of Reading, Types of Reading, Causes and Remedies of Reading Failures, Reading Techniques & Strategies (Scanning, Skimming, Phrase reading, Intensive & Extensive reading, Exploiting the topic sentence for main ideas), Reading for details, Reading for evaluation and inference, Reading with questions - SQ3R, PR3, Methods for understanding difficult words in a reading text, Literature reading for study, analysis and comment.

Speaking & Communication Skills - Nature, Process & Development, Principles of Public Speech Making and Social Interaction, The Speech Sounds of English and their Articulation, Phonetic Transcription and Practical Speech Work.

Study Techniques - Choosing study centers and discussion groups, Note-taking during lectures, and from audio-visual equipment, Note-making techniques during private reading and literature search, Summary & Transcoding Techniques, Retrieving information from notes, The dictionary as a study guide.

Basic Research Methods & Term Paper Writing - Research – meaning & nature, Types & Methodology; Data in the Research Process, The Research Report, Process and Techniques, Documentation in Research Reports: Process, Types and Methods, Abbreviations in Research Reports, The term paper as a miniature research report, Practical term paper writing.

Course Evaluation & Grading - Students must attend at least 75% of the lectures to qualify for examination in the course.', topics = '["Man, Society and Language - The Nature, Characteristics and Functions of Language, Human Communication & Language, World English, Levels and Varieties of English", "Vocabulary of English - Types, Method of Vocabulary Development, Synonyms, Antonyms, Homonyms, Acronyms, Paronyms, Affixation and other morphological processes", "Listening skill - Nature, Types, Purposes and Factors that affect Listening, Strategies and Aids for Effective Listening", "Reading Skill - Reading Problems, Levels and Types of Reading, Causes and Remedies of Reading Failures, Reading Techniques & Strategies, Reading for evaluation and inference", "Speaking & Communication Skills - Principles of Public Speech Making and Social Interaction, Phonetic Transcription and Practical Speech Work", "Study Techniques - Note-taking, Note-making, Summary & Transcoding Techniques", "Basic Research Methods & Term Paper Writing - The Research Report, Documentation, Abbreviations, practical term paper writing"]'::jsonb
 where course_code = 'GSP 101' and department = 'Metallurgical and Materials Engineering';

update public.course_outlines
   set course_title = 'Basic Grammar and Varieties of Writing', description = '(Description and topics reused from Computer Science''s outline for the same course.) Part A: Basic Grammar: Introduction. The concept of grammar and its place in language teaching and learning. Parts of speech and their functions (treated in detail). Closed and open class items in parts of speech, Nominalization, Grammatical Structures: the phrase, the clause and the sentence. Elementary Clause Analysis, Sentence Types, Elements and Patterns. Agreement (Grammatical agreement, Notional agreement, Proximity agreement) Agreement with the correlatives. Direct and Reported Speech, Error typology identification and correction.

Part B: Varieties of writing. Introduction (The Meaning, Nature and Purpose of Writing, Writing Types or Genres and their Characteristics). The paragraph as the basic unit of an essay (Types, Development of the Paragraph, Methods of Paragraph Development, The thesis statement). Point of view and style in writing. Qualities of a good piece of writing: Form, Diction and Content in writing. The Mechanics of Writing: punctuation, spelling and capitalization.

Part C: Writing Genres - Planning and choosing your theme. Deciding your genre. Choosing and developing your plot. Point of view, setting and characterization. Using the language that works. Essay Writing — Narration, Description, Exposition and Argumentation. Technical Writing: Letter Writing, Memorandum Writing, Speech Writing, Agenda and Minutes, own story for practice, Computer-linked writing, types, style, language, and process.', topics = '["Part A: Basic Grammar - The concept of grammar, Parts of speech, Grammatical Structures, Sentence Types, Agreement, Direct and Reported Speech, Error typology", "Part B: Varieties of writing - Meaning, Nature and Purpose of Writing, the paragraph as the basic unit of an essay, the thesis statement, Qualities of a good piece of writing, Mechanics of Writing", "Part C: Writing Genres - Planning and choosing your theme, plot, point of view, setting and characterization", "Essay Writing - Narration, Description, Exposition and Argumentation", "Technical Writing - Letter Writing, Memorandum Writing, Speech Writing, Agenda and Minutes"]'::jsonb
 where course_code = 'GSP 102' and department = 'Agricultural and Bioresources Engineering';

